 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? They' worth it if you don't enjoy planning weddings yourself. A good planner takes a lot of stress out of the day and makes sure everything runs smoothly. Then a wedding planner can keep the room from getting cluttered, keep everyone on track, and make sure the important bits don't get missed. It usually means the morning of the big day, so the groom can practice getting ready without the family around. It' worth every penny if it gives you peace of mind. That's understandable. Maybe offer her the role of matron of honour instead, she gets to wear a lovely dress and she's important too.",
